   "text": "This SMILES was read from the drawing region by region. It has not been checked with a parser, and two choices below are inferences rather than clear readings.\n\n- **Biotin end:** a biotin unit carries the stereochemistry I copied from the standard D-(+)-biotin SMILES. Its valeric acid chain is acylated by an amino-PEG3 linker: NH\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2\u2013C(=O).\n- **Macrocycle:** the linker acylates the N-terminus of a propargylglycine residue. That residue's side chain is a 1,4-disubstituted 1,2,3-triazole, whose N1 carries a four-carbon chain back to a lysine-derived residue (an azidolysine) at the other end of the ring. The ring sequence runs from the propargylglycine C=O through Lys, Lys, Gly, Trp (indol-3-yl side chain), Pro and the azidolysine. The azidolysine ends in a primary amide, C(=O)NH2. Each Lys side chain is a free (CH2)4NH2.\n- **Stereochemistry:** I counted four CH2 groups between the triazole N1 and the azidolysine \u03b1-carbon. All amino acid centres are drawn with wedges. For the propargylglycine and the first Lys I checked the geometry by hand and found L. I assumed L for the remaining residues, assigned each @/@@ to match, and did not verify any of them independently.\n\nSMILES: C1[C@H]2[C@@H]([C@@H](S1)CCCCC(=O)NCCOCCOCCOCC(=O)N[C@@H](Cc1cn(nn1)CCCC[C@@H](C(N)=O)NC(=O)[C@@H]1CCCN1C(=O)[C@H](Cc3c[nH]c4ccccc34)NC(=O)CNC(=O)[C@H](CCCCN)NC(=O)[C@H](CCCCN)N9)C9=O)NC(=O)N2"
